<h1>The question comes home</h1><<ownAssessment>><details><summary>Sources, reading boundary, and credits</summary><p>Miguel de Cervantes, Don Quixote, translated by John Ormsby (1885), Project Gutenberg eBook 996, public domain.</p><p>Reading boundary: Part I, chapter 1: opening portrait, reading habits, armor and helmet, naming Rocinante and Don Quixote, ending with Dulcinea. No later plot revealed.</p><p>Checked 2026-10-10. Original dialogue, student appointment, journal magic, and Cervantes margin visits are authored fiction. Labelled source cards alone contain authentic excerpts. Author, narrator, and character voices are distinct. These are episode concepts; a current assigned weekly vocabulary list and class translation were not verified. Read the assigned class text as well. No live AI responses.</p><p>Episode concepts: characterization, diction, parody. Original 16-bit art generated with OpenAI imagegen. Optional quiet retro music generated with MusicGen-Looper; an artistic atmosphere, not a historical reconstruction. Details in the repository source record.</p><<ownSource>></details><<button "Replay with a new question">><<if window.parent===window>><<run setup.choices=[];setup.driverAttempts=[];setup.journal={};setup.drafts={};setup.accepted=false;setup.attemptId=crypto.randomUUID();setup.refresh()>><<else>><<run setup.send("replay")>><</if>><</button>><<button "Return to The Game">><<if window.parent===window>><p>My class account provides the game library and saved attempts.</p><<else>><<run setup.send("exit")>><</if>><</button>>
